cli.flow.run_heading:
run {run_id} — flow {flow} — {status}
steps: {total} ({went} went, {broke} broke)
calls: {calls}

cli.flow.schedule_written:
flow {flow} ({origin}): trigger
  from: {before}
  to:   {after}
written in {directory}

cli.flow.past_models_unpriced:
models used by past runs that the price list cannot price: {models}
  their cost stays unknown, not zero: the counted spend is lower than the real one
  it is repaired by writing the entry in ~/.config/sailor/pricing.json, which wins over the shipped one

cli.flow.paths_inside_text_to_fix_by_han:
TO FIX BY HAND — paths inside a text, {count} in all:
  {paths}
They are not rewritten: a prompt is an instruction, and rewriting it is deciding it.

cli.step.taken_on:
step {step_id} taken on by «{holder}» — run {run_id}, attempt {attempt}
── brief ──
{mandate}
──
when you are done: sailor step close --run {run_id} --step {step_id} --as {holder} --outcome went [--output-file <file>] [--turns <n>]

cli.workspace.written:
wrote {file}
  name: {name}
  rules: {rules}
  checks: none (they are written by hand: guessing them would be deciding them for you)
